# W4-NEXT-1 part U rows 5 and 10 (orchestrator review finding 6, 2026-11-10): captures the live
# window's own drawing for demolish mode (the pickaxe's active frame) and the pause overlay, for
# ui_dynamic_draw_check.py's pixel comparison against the UI.1 oracle - construction_menu_draw_
# check.script's own idle/public/roads captures never turn either flag on.
#
# B is overloaded under --construction-menu on (viewer.cpp's construction_handle, ADR 0004 R1):
# the first B (menu closed) opens the construction menu and is consumed there, never reaching the
# developer tool's own B-toggle; only the SECOND B (menu already open) falls through to enable
# the tool, which X (ToggleDemolish) needs (sdl_input.cpp: every tool key but B returns nullopt
# while the tool is disabled). One B alone looked like it worked (no error) but left X a no-op,
# so the first version of this script silently captured the idle pickaxe and compared against
# itself - caught only by this script's own deliberately-wrong-input control failing to be
# rejected (both sides were the same idle sprite).
resize 1024 768
wait frames 5
key b
wait frames 5
key b
wait frames 5
key x
wait frames 5
screenshot construction_demolish_live
key x
key esc
wait frames 5
# toggle_pause() marks the window dirty once (viewer.cpp) but the scene then stops animating,
# so no further frames redraw on their own - "wait frames 5" here would hang until
# ANNO_VIEW_QUIT_S force-quits; the one triggered redraw is already enough to show the overlay.
key space
wait frames 1
screenshot hud_paused_live
key space
wait frames 1
quit
